    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Chemistry</span> is the branch of science that studies the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">composition, structure, properties, and changes</span> of matter. It is often called the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">central science</span> because it connects other natural sciences such as physics, biology, geology, and environmental science.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Definition and Scope</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Chemistry is the scientific study of matter, its properties, the changes it undergoes, and the energy involved in those changes. Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Brief History</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Robert Boyle (1627–1691):</strong> Distinguished chemistry from alchemy; formulated Boyle's Law.</li>\n  <li><strong>Antoine Lavoisier (1743–1794):</strong> \"Father of Modern Chemistry\"; discovered oxygen's role in combustion.</li>\n  <li><strong>John Dalton (1766–1844):</strong> Proposed the atomic theory of matter.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dmitri Mendeleev (1834–1907):</strong> Developed the Periodic Table.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Branches of Chemistry</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Branch</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Organic Chemistry</td><td>Carbon-containing compounds</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inorganic Chemistry</td><td>Non-carbon compounds; metals, minerals</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Physical Chemistry</td><td>Energy and physical properties in reactions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Analytical Chemistry</td><td>Identifying and measuring substances</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Biochemistry</td><td>Chemical processes in living organisms</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Industrial Chemistry</td><td>Large-scale chemical production</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance of Chemistry</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Medicine:</strong> Development of drugs and vaccines.</li>\n  <li><strong>Agriculture:</strong> Fertilisers and pesticides improve yields.</li>\n  <li><strong>Industry:</strong> Manufacture of plastics, textiles, metals, and fuels.</li>\n  <li><strong>Environment:</strong> Understanding and reducing pollution.</li>\n  <li><strong>Food Science:</strong> Preservation and nutritional analysis.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Antoine Lavoisier is the \"Father of Modern Chemistry\" — a popular exam question. Know the six branches and their focus areas.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Chemistry is the study of matter, its composition, properties, and transformations. It has six main branches and is important in medicine, agriculture, industry, food science, and environmental protection.\n</div>\n  ",
