    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">chemical laboratory</span> is a specially equipped room for conducting experiments safely. The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">chemical industry</span> uses chemical processes on a large scale to manufacture useful products. Knowing laboratory apparatus and their correct uses is fundamental to practical chemistry.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Common Laboratory Apparatus and Uses</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Apparatus</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Beaker</td><td>Holding and heating liquids; mixing solutions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Conical (Erlenmeyer) Flask</td><td>Mixing and heating; used in titrations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Test tube</td><td>Carrying out small-scale reactions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Burette</td><td>Delivering accurate volumes of liquid in titrations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Pipette</td><td>Transferring a fixed accurate volume of liquid</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Measuring cylinder</td><td>Measuring approximate volumes of liquids</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Volumetric flask</td><td>Preparing standard solutions of exact volume</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Bunsen burner</td><td>Heating substances in the laboratory</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Condenser</td><td>Cooling vapour back to liquid during distillation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Tripod stand and wire gauze</td><td>Supporting glassware above a flame</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Evaporating dish</td><td>Evaporating solvent to obtain a solid solute</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Crucible</td><td>Strongly heating substances at high temperatures</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Watch glass</td><td>Covering beakers; small-scale evaporation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Safety Rules in the Laboratory</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Always wear protective clothing: lab coat, goggles, and gloves.</li>\n  <li>Never taste or smell chemicals directly.</li>\n  <li>Label all reagent bottles correctly.</li>\n  <li>Never point a heated test tube at anyone.</li>\n  <li>Know the location of fire extinguishers and first aid kits.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Chemical Industries in Nigeria</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Petroleum refining:</strong> NNPC refineries in Warri, Port Harcourt, and Kaduna.</li>\n  <li><strong>Fertiliser production:</strong> Notore Chemical Industries produces urea and ammonia-based fertilisers.</li>\n  <li><strong>Cement industry:</strong> Dangote Cement and others produce Portland cement.</li>\n  <li><strong>Pharmaceutical industry:</strong> Companies produce drugs such as paracetamol and antimalarials.</li>\n  <li><strong>Textile/Dye industry:</strong> Uses chemical dyes and bleaches to colour fabrics.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the difference between burette and pipette. A burette measures variable volumes; a pipette measures a single fixed volume. The volumetric flask is used only for preparing standard solutions.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Laboratory apparatus each have specific purposes. Safety rules are essential. Nigeria's chemical industries include petroleum refining, fertilisers, cement, pharmaceuticals, and textiles.\n</div>\n  ",
